megadap-etz21-pro-e-to-z-mount-adapter-review-viable-but-not-vindicated 
Someone decided to allow E-mount lenses to be mounted onto Nikon bodies.

We got our hands on the ETZ21 Pro, which costs something, to see if E-mount lenses play nice with Nikon bodies.

Sony E-mount lenses have a physical lens mount diameter in a certain state.

E-mount lenses can fit, with a very thin adapter, and still function in a certain way on the sensor plane.

We were fortunate to have someone donate an ETZ21 Pro adapter for testing.

The adapter locked into place firmly on the something that we tested. 
The Megadap ETZ21 Pro makes sense for photographers dumping Sony cameras to switch to Nikon but still possessing a significant investment in E-mount glass.

The Megadap ETZ21 Pro makes sense for photographers who own both Sony and Nikon systems and want to mix lenses.

The Megadap adapter works surprisingly seamlessly for mounting E-glass onto Nikon bodies.

